    {
      "id": "6a15472c564f4ca152670471",
      "title": "3D Mini Me",
      "slug": "3d-mini-me-figurine",
      "category": "CGI & 3D Modeling",
      "category_slug": "cgi-3d-modeling",
      "prompt": "Use the uploaded photo as the ONLY identity reference. Preserve exact facial structure, proportions, skin tone, hairstyle, eye shape, nose, lips, jawline, and overall identity with high accuracy. Do not beautify, alter, or replace facial features.\nCreate a photorealistic 4:5 portrait of the subject seated on the left side of the frame, at a wooden artist’s desk. The framing is mid-torso upward, with the subject slightly angled toward the camera while maintaining direct eye contact and a warm, natural smile. One forearm rests casually on the desk, creating a relaxed and approachable posture.\nOn the desk beside the subject (clearly visible but not blocking the subject), place a high-quality 3D animated miniature version of the same person, standing on a clear circular base. The miniature must be a Pixar/Disney-style stylized version of the subject — slightly exaggerated proportions, large expressive eyes, and a polished, premium 3D look — while still maintaining clear resemblance to the real person. Outfit, hairstyle, and colors must match exactly.\nThe environment is a cozy artist workspace: include a realistic paint palette with mixed colors, small paint jars, a glass holder filled with brushes, scattered brushes, and sketch papers on the desk.\nLighting is primarily from a black articulated desk lamp, casting a warm, soft, diffused glow across the subject and the miniature. Add subtle ambient fill light to maintain natural skin tones and soft shadows. Ensure smooth falloff and no harsh contrast.\nBackground should be softly blurred (shallow depth of field), featuring a corkboard with pinned pencil sketches and subtle studio elements, maintaining depth without distraction.\nRendering style must be ultra-clean and premium:\n\nPhotorealistic skin texture, natural lighting, soft shadows, high dynamic range. The 3D miniature should have clean Pixar-style materials, smooth shading, and no plastic or toy-like cheap appearance. Seamlessly blend real photography with high-end 3D character integration.\nCinematic color grading, 50mm lens look, f/1.8 depth of field, sharp focus on subject and miniature, ultra-detailed, 8K quality.\nNegative Prompt:\nanime, 2D illustration, cartoon background, flat shading, low poly, plastic toy look, waxy skin, face swap, different identity, face morphing, beautified face, over-smoothing, blur, low resolution, grain, noise, distortion, deformed face, incorrect proportions, extra fingers, missing fingers, duplicated limbs, floating objects, bad anatomy, inconsistent lighting, harsh shadows, neon lighting, cold tones, over-saturation, washed colors, watermark, text, logo, cropped face, miniature body crop, out-of-frame subject",
      "description": "Mini Me Photo Prompt: Use this prompt to generate a professional studio image of a person sitting alongside a matching 3D cartoon figurine in an artist's workspace.",
      "ai_tools": [
        "Gemini"
      ],
      "like_count": 133,
